      <Desc>IN SUMMER 2024, THE CALIFORNIA STATE GAMES HOSTED THE STATE GAMES OF AMERICA, A BIENNIAL EVENT THAT INVITES MEDALISTS FROM ALL NATIONAL CONGRESS OF STATE GAMES MEMBER STATES (APPROXIMATELY 30 STATES) FROM THE PREVIOUS TWO YEARS TO COMPETE IN A NATIONAL COMPETITION. THE LAST TIME THE CALIFORNIA STATE GAMES HOSTED THE STATE GAMES OF AMERICA WAS IN 2011. THE 2024 STATE GAMES OF AMERICA INCLUDED ARCHERY, ARTISTIC SWIMMING, BADMINTON, BASKETBALL, BMX RACING, CLIMBING, CURLING, DIVING, FIELD HOCKEY. FIGURE SKATING (ISI &amp; USFS), FOOTGOLF, JUDO, NINJA CLIMBING, PICKLEBALL, RUGBY, SKATEBOARDING, SOFTBALL, SURFING, SWIMMING (SHORT COURSE &amp; LONG COURSE), TRACK &amp; FIELD, WATER POLO, WRESTLING, AND YOGA. UNLIKE TYPICAL YEARS WHERE ATHLETES COME FROM CALIFORNIA AND NEIGHBORING STATES, THE STATE GAMES OF AMERICA WELCOMED ATHLETES FROM OVER 20 STATES IN SUMMER 2024 TO SAN DIEGO.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>121622</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>202669</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>THE 2024 CALIFORNIA WINTER GAMES WAS HELD IN SAN DIEGO IN FEBRUARY &amp; MARCH. PARTICIPATING WERE 1,971 ATHLETES COMPETING IN 4 SPORTS. THE OBJECTIVE OF THE CAL WINTER GAMES IS TO HOST A HIGH-QUALITY SPORTS EVENT THAT INCLUDES ATHLETES FROM NOT ONLY CALIFORNIA BUT THROUGHOUT THE US. THE SPORTS INCLUDED WERE CURLING, FIGURE SKATING, ICE HOCKEY &amp; GYMNASTICS.</Desc>
